{"skill":{"slug":"browsh","displayName":"browsh"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1768936491160,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":848,"sha256":"24db613bf79de40329b5a4634cd7566f9bda17975dc2c993e23148fd8be84268","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1604,"sha256":"a523d7753ac4228551d35676e60db4b6c11b54861efb0b9aa3212d9558a67eae","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016693505,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"15932400778973d304bdcf0102613091656ba5daae756ea058ff773dd78b5b35","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/15932400778973d304bdcf0102613091656ba5daae756ea058ff773dd78b5b35","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: browsh\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle describes how to use the 'browsh' text-based browser, requiring 'browsh' and 'firefox' binaries. The `SKILL.md` provides standard usage instructions and a common `export PATH` command for local setup, which is not inherently malicious. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection with harmful intent against the agent. The content is clearly aligned with the stated purpose of running a text-based browser.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159808290},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789016693505},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill only documents how to run Browsh, a terminal web browser that uses Firefox, and its requested behavior matches that purpose.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of a PTY and Firefox backend is proportionate for a terminal browser; no broad filesystem indexing, credential access, or privileged local mutation is requested.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No installer is bundled. The skill assumes browsh and firefox are already installed and optionally shows a local PATH export for binaries under ~/apps.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are limited to prerequisites, an optional PATH example, and direct Browsh usage; there are no hidden role changes, prompt overrides, or unrelated agent instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact does not create services, scheduled tasks, persistent hooks, memory entries, or privilege escalation paths.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill describes Browsh as a text-based browser and provides commands to start it or open a URL; browser network access and headless Firefox use are expected for that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, confirm you trust and have installed the browsh and firefox binaries separately. Running Browsh will browse the web through Firefox, which is expected for this skill.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016693505}}}}}